# .graphifyignore — Graphify knowledge-graph exclusions for SpecterStudio (AWKIT)
#
# Graphify honors .gitignore first; this file is evaluated after it and adds the
# TRACKED files that add no value to a code/architecture graph (large media, binary
# assets, package-lock, tracker exports) plus a defence-in-depth repeat of the
# sensitive patterns already in .gitignore.
#
# Uses .gitignore syntax. Top-level runtime dirs are ROOT-ANCHORED (leading "/")
# because real SOURCE dirs share their names (src/reports/, src/profiles/,
# src/storage/, src/data/, src/instances/, app/renderer/components/reports/).
# Same rationale as .cbmignore — see docs/ai/CODEBASE-MEMORY-AND-BEADS.md.
#
# Refresh procedure and what IS indexed: docs/ai/GRAPHIFY.md.

# --- Graphify's own output and vendored skill docs (never index the tool into the graph) ---
# AWKIT's OWN skills under .claude/skills/ (git-full-cycle, mock-site-maintainer, …) ARE
# authoritative project instructions and stay indexed — only graphify's vendored copy is excluded.
/graphify-out/
/.claude/skills/graphify/

# --- Dependencies & package-manager metadata ---
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/
/package-lock.json

# --- Build / bundle / packaging output ---
/dist/
/build/
/out/
/release/
.vite/
.cache/
.temp/
/electron-builder/
*.asar
# Generated timestamped electron-vite configs (source of truth is electron.vite.config.ts)
electron.vite.config.*.mjs

# --- Bundled offline runtime (large binaries: Chromium, native modules, JDBC jars) ---
/vendor/
/.release-local/
resources/browsers/
resources/oracle-jdbc/runtime/
resources/oracle-jdbc/bridge/
resources/oracle-jdbc/lib/
# Compiled Java bridge artifacts (source under oracle-jdbc-bridge/src stays indexed)
oracle-jdbc-bridge/target/

